# Line endings: the shell scripts must be LF even on Windows.
#
# Git for Windows ships `core.autocrlf=true`, so a plain checkout hands out the
# `bin/*.sh` scripts with CRLF. A CRLF shebang makes Git Bash answer
# `$'\r': command not found` for every line of `watchd.sh`, so the watcher never
# starts and the only symptom is a stale `state/health.json`
# (INSTALL.md §6, runbook `supervisor-daemon.md` Windows section).
# `bin/selfcheck.py` fails a CRLF script too, so this cannot regress silently.
*.sh text eol=lf
